{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "murmur-gate4-massive-dark-metallic-bass",
    "name": "MASSIVE DARK EVOLVING METALLIC BASS",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "GATE 4 acceptance patch (see docs/ROADMAP.md 'GATE 4'): built entirely from real, already-implemented DSP -- no unison DSP (not wired yet, ROADMAP Phase 7) and no dedicated FM/Resonator engine (silent, Phase 10 PLANNED). MASSIVE via 3 hand-detuned saws (ratios 0.996/1.0/1.004, the same fake-unison technique wide-saw.pw8 already established) plus two centered sub sines (ratio 0.5 and 0.25) for controlled low end. DARK via Filter 1 lowpass at 350Hz. METALLIC via a genuine RING_MOD algorithm-graph edge (node0, a non-output 3.17-ratio triangle, ring-modulates node1, a dedicated low-level 1.5-ratio saw) -- inharmonic ring-mod partials layered in as a controlled texture voice, not applied to the fundamental. EVOLVING via LFO1 -> FilterCutoff (slow sweep) and LFO1 -> OperatorLevel(node1) (the metallic voice swells in and out over time) plus Velocity -> FilterCutoff for hit-hard velocity response. A single Saturation insert (drive 10dB) adds harmonic weight before any mastering.",
    "category": "bass",
    "moods": [
      "dark",
      "massive",
      "metallic",
      "evolving"
    ],
    "genres": [],
